From e227596240c016ddcbbc95db40cb4bdcba8c9deb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:15:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7996: Fix memory allocation failure handling in
 MURU config

Problem:
Memory allocation failure for the MURU configuration structure can
lead to unexpected behavior when setting MURU parameters, potentially
causing system instability.

Root Cause:
The code does not check for successful memory allocation of the MURU
structure, leading to potential null pointer dereference if allocation
fails.

Solution:
Add a check for the result of kzalloc and return -ENOMEM if memory
allocation for the MURU structure fails, preventing null pointer
dereference and ensuring stable operation.

Feature:
Stability

Signed-off-by: Howard Hsu <howard-yh.hsu@mediatek.com>
---
 mt7996/mtk_mcu.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7996/mtk_mcu.c b/mt7996/mtk_mcu.c
index f1a48ecfb..baa0eab24 100644
--- a/mt7996/mtk_mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mtk_mcu.c
@@ -1192,6 +1192,9 @@ int mt7996_set_muru_cfg(struct mt7996_dev *dev, u8 action, u8 val)
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	muru = kzalloc(sizeof(struct mt7996_muru), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!muru)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+
 	dl = &muru->dl;
 	ul = &muru->ul;
 	comm = &muru->comm;
-- 
2.45.2

